<BaseLayout title="Coaching" description="One-on-one strength coaching for powerlifters and serious lifters.">
  <article class="prose">
    <h1>Coaching</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      I coach a small number of lifters at a time. If what I write here resonates
      and you want someone in your corner, read on.
    </p>

    <h2>Who it's for</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Powerlifters prepping for a meet, or thinking about their first</li>
      <li>Lifters whose numbers have stalled and who want a plan, not another program</li>
      <li>People who already know the basics and want sharper execution</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Who it's not for</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Beginners looking for Starting Strength — you'll get more mileage from the free program</li>
      <li>Anyone looking for a cookie-cutter template they'll follow for 12 weeks</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>How it works</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>
        <strong>Intake call.</strong> 30 minutes, free. We talk about your training,
        your meet plans, your schedule, what's been working and what hasn't.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Program + weekly check-ins.</strong> I write your program and we
        review it every week over video or by async notes — whichever you prefer.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Logging via <a href="/powertrack">PowerTrack</a>.</strong> You get
        a free account on the training app I built. I see your sessions as you log
        them.
      </li>
    </ol>

    <h2>Pricing</h2>
    <p>[Replace with your pricing. Flat monthly, meet-prep block, or whatever makes sense for how you want to run this.]</p>

    <h2>Ready?</h2>
    <p>
      <a href="mailto:you@remoratechnical.com?subject=Coaching%20intake">
        Email me to book the intake call →
      </a>
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
